invariant: INV-39
file: handshake_post.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_read rekeys on a KeyUpdate that has bytes after it in its
  record and reads on, in either role. colibri sent a server one record
  holding two KeyUpdates, and a message that starts after a KeyUpdate
  finishes under the next key. RFC 9846 section 5.1 makes that
  unexpected_message. test/session_record_end_tests.h holds the KeyUpdate
  that ends its record and the one with a byte after it.

--- old
    if (!ends_input) {
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
    if (t->key_update_run >= CH_KEY_UPDATE_RUN_MAX) {
--- new
    (void)ends_input;
    if (t->key_update_run >= CH_KEY_UPDATE_RUN_MAX) {
